{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1487247-trinity-continuum-\u00e6ther-and-victorian-mage","id":1487247,"title":"Trinity Continuum: \u00c6ther and Victorian Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T13:54:11-07:00","id":1487247,"title":"Trinity Continuum: \u00c6ther and Victorian Mage","content":"So: the current Kickstarter for Trinity Continuum is \u00c6ther. Set in the late 19th century, it depicts a world where a reality altering substance known as \u00c6ther is discovered in the middle of the 19th century and revolutionizes science. \u00c6ther explicitly takes the intent of the \u00c6thernaut into account in terms of just how it changes reality. <br /> <br /> I have long been of the belief that it would be easy to incorporate elements of Mage into Trinity Continuum's Adventure era (pre-WWII) by the simple expedient of replacing the Hammersmith Event that kickstarted the Inspired with Czar Vargo. But this? This is even <i>easier</i>. Combining the settings of TC: \u00c6ther and Victorian Mage is as simple as saying that the Electrodyne Engineers jumped ship a couple of decades early, or gained a stronger place within the Order of Reason to the point that they were able to push their own agenda much more effectively. <br /> <br /> So: viewing TC: \u00c6ther as a radically different Future Fate for Victorian Mage, which then goes on to develop in parallel to Adventure, Assassins, Aberrant, Anima, and \u00c6on, how would you see Mage society reacting to these developments? That is, instead of the setting being \u201clike our world, but with hidden supernatural elements\u201d, what if the setting is \u201clike the Trinity Continuum, but with hidden supernatural elements\u201d? <br /> <br /> (The mechanics of getting Victorian Mage and TC: \u00c6ther to play nice under one set of rules is a separate issue, which has more broadly been addressed in other posts here. I'm mainly interested in how the settings would combine, both in the short term and in the long term.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T14:13:30-07:00","id":1487250,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to blend the two settings. Victorian Mage and Aether are clearly a lovely pairing. Picture the Order of Reason comes apart and the Order of Hermes reaches out to the Electrodyne Engineers. Bringing the EE into the Council and using new visions of the future to undermine the Order of Reason's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T14:54:21-07:00","id":1487508,"title":"","content":"Initial thoughts: <br /> <br /> TC: \u00c6ther has a few elements in it that diverge from real-world history long before the discovery of \u00c6ther; most notably the Immortals, who have been around for centuries. It also plays a bit fast and loose with timeline considerations, with the likes of Dr. Jekyll, Moriarty, and Dorian Gray still being alive long after the dates in fiction that they supposedly died. For this fusion, I'm thinking of setting the <i>actual</i> \u201cdivergence point\u201d, not in 1880 when Nikola Tesla discovered the \u00c6ther, but in 1859 when a Cosian diagnosed and cured Prince Albert's stomach cramps, leading to him <i>not</i> dying in 1861 and still being alive all the way through into the \u00c6theric Age. (He was 42 when he died; so had he survived, he would have been 76 at the start of the Martian invasion.)<br /> <br /> This changes the history of the Order of Reason: somewhere between 1861 and 1880, Albert meets the Etherite faction within the Electrodyne Engineers and learns of their Ether Science. He becomes a proponent of it, leading to Nikola Tesla's Discovery of the \u00c6ther in 1880. From there, the history of the two settings develop in tandem until the end of the Martian invasion. <br /> <br /> I'm assuming that the \u00c6ther Age will end with many \u00c6thernauts and their Spinnings getting Unwound, with the former becoming fictional characters as a result. The near disaster turns the Union against the \u00c6ther, though it won't be until Tychoides develops his Cosmology model almost a decade later in 1905 that the Union will be able to put forward an alternative, leading to the formal rejection of Ether by the Union and the Sons of Ether walking. In 1914, Czar Vargo attempts to end World War I before it begins, but is defeated by High Scientist Michael Faraday (who sacrifices his life to stop Vargo). Finally, in 1921, we get the Hammersmith Incident; and the world is forever changed. Hammersmith, in this blending, was a Son of Ether, attempting to restart the \u00c6ther Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T17:37:00-07:00","id":1487521,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a longer lifespan for Prince Albert &quot;The Good&quot; as the snarky ones called him. Would change the character of the Kaiser. Also a Cosian might cure the Kaiser's dad (and for that matter the Kaiser). Kaiser Bill's dad died of throat cancer. Extend the man's life thirty years and the Kaiser is middle aged when he becomes Emperor. As Kaiser Bill's dad strongly believed in human rights and constitutional government, thirty years of his influence might mean the Kaiser is not even really important.<br /> <br /> And if the Kaiser had two good arms and could participate in the kind of life he admired and clearly wanted maybe he's a more stable and thoughtful man. Or at least doesn't feel a desperate need to overcompensate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-22-2022, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T19:53:25-07:00","id":1487535,"title":"","content":"Hopefully not <i>too</i> much of a change. It's fine imagining better alternate histories; but one of the goals here is to remain reasonably close to the primary TC timeline. We don't want something that derails WWI, much as it would be nice if it could be avoided; because it <i>wasn't</i> avoided in TC. <br /> <br /> Mainly what I'm wanting to do with Albert is to change the character of the Technocracy enough to make it more compatible with the science-positive world of TC, by having Albert there in its early days to rein in some of its worst excesses. Something so that, when we get to TC: Adventure!, significant parts of the TU are part of its whole Hope theme. That, and to give a reason behind \u00c6ther being accepted by the Order of Reason from 1880 to 1895 \u2014 with the knock-on effect of it still having more adherents even within the Union, and even after it's officially banned: once you've let the genie out of the bottle, it's nigh on impossible to put it back in. <br /> <br /> I even briefly considered a possibility where there's still enough underground support for the \u00c6ther in the post-1905 Union that the Etherites don't jump ship; and their place in the Traditions gets taken by the Ngoma. Why the Ngoma? Because they've always had something of a technomantic bent to them (in terms of real-world Bantu beliefs, even if that was omitted from their original write-up in Sorcerers Crusade Companion); and I could easily see that amplified by incorporating the Zulu Mechanists, the Awalaye, and the Wamukamwami into their ranks (for reference: Victorian Mage describes the Awalaye and the Wamukamwami as loose confederations of Central African medicine people and doctors, with their own competing Sciences which included effective medical practices and precise future prediction; and in the latter case, an understanding of Etheric Mechanics that was possibly superior to that of the Sons of Ether). So I could see an alternate history where the \u201cweird science\u201d fraction of the Traditions has <i>no</i> connection to the Technocracy, and has distinctly Central African roots. <br /> <br /> But that's not TC, either. Not so early in its timeline, at least. I could see something like that by the time of TC: \u00c6on, though, with its \u201cAfrica: the Bright Continent\u201d thing going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-23-2022, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}